<title>RUSSIA: Russian railway freight charges to fall from Oct.</title>
<headline>Russian railway freight charges to fall from Oct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia plans to cut railway freight and cargo rates by five percent from October 1, government spokesman Igor Shabdurasulov said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Starting October 1, 1997, freight railway rates and rates for cargo handling work should be reduced by five percent compared with those that will be in effect in September 1997,&quot; he told a news briefing.</p>
<p>Many Russian raw materials and finished and semi-finished goods are shipped by rail because roads are poor or non-existent. Rivers and canals can only be used during the summer months.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
